s terminals (T1) and non-terminals (T2, T3). So Outside Hand would require all melds and pair to have terminals or honors. The T1-T2-T3 includes T2 and T3 which are not terminals. So Outside Hand is not possible.\n\nHmm. Maybe the best is to discard F4 now and try to form other patterns. If I discard F4, I can keep other tiles. For example, if I discard F4, my hand is W1, W2, W4, B5, B7, F2. Then, maybe form other melds. For example, if I can form a Chow of W1-W2-W3, but the W3s are in the Kong. No. Or form a pair of W4s? No, only one. So maybe not helpful.\n\nAlternatively, if I discard B5, keeping F4. Let's say I discard B5. Then, if I later draw an F4, I can make a Pung. That would give 2 points. Plus the concealed Kong (4), total 6. Still need 2 more. Maybe another pattern like All Chows? If I can form four Chows and a pair. But with the current hand, it's not clear.\n\nAnother thought: since I have a concealed Kong of W3s, that's 4 points. If I can form a Pung of F4s (2 points), and another pattern like All Honors (if all tiles are honors). But I have W1, W2, W4, which are not honors. So no.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the hand can form a Seven Pairs. But with the melds taking up 7 tiles, and the hand having 6, it's not possible. Need 7 pairs (14 tiles). So no.\n\nSo maybe the best is to discard a tile that's not useful, like B5 or B7. Let's go with discarding B5. But wait, in the valid actions, Play B5 is an option. Wait, no, the valid actions are Play B5; Play F4; etc. So to discard a tile, I need to play it. So if I want to discard B5, I choose Play B5. Similarly for others.\n\nSo the decision is between Play B5, Play B7, Play F2, etc. Considering the potential for forming a Pung of F4s, it's better to keep F4. So discard B5 or B7.\n\nBetween B5 and B7, which has more remaining? B5 has 3 left, B7 has 2. So B7 is less available. Discarding B7 might be better because it's less likely to be needed by others. But since B6 is gone, B7 can't be part of a B5-B6-B7 Chow. So maybe B7 is not useful. So discard B7.\n\nAlternatively, discard F2. F2 is a single, not part of any pattern. So that's safe.\n\nBut the best move is probably to discard B5 or B7. Let's say I discard B5. Then, if I can get another F4, that's better. So the answer would be Play B5.\n", "output": "Evaluation: [Discard B5 to retain potential for forming a Pung of F4s (Seat Wind and Prevalent Wind) and avoid holding terminal tiles (B7) that are less useful due to B6 being exhausted. The concealed Kong of W3s already provides 4 points, and a Pung of F4s could add 2 points toward the 8-point minimum.]\nReason: [B5 is less critical than F4 for scoring, as F4 is the Seat Wind and Prevalent Wind. Discarding B5 preserves the chance to complete a Pung of F4s, which would add 2 points. B7 is also a candidate, but B5 has more remaining tiles (3 vs. 2), making it a safer discard.]\nAnswer: Play B5"}
